      "name": "Shazad Nazir",
      "created_at": "2025-09-25T11:03:06.879Z",
      "cooked": "<p>While finishing a Work Order for a batch-enabled Finished Good in ERPNext v15, we noticed an issue with manual batch creation. When the system generates the Stock Entry (Manufacture) against a work order and we create a new batch using the “Add Batch” option in the Finished Goods section and create a new batch, the batch is successfully created but does not appear in the batch dropdown list in that very same window (where I was just created).</p>\n<p>As a result, we are unable to assign the newly created batch to the Finished Goods item in Stock Entry (Manufacture) Add Batch window.</p>\n<p>On the other hand, when we enable <strong>Auto Batch Creation</strong> in item master of the same Finished Good, the process works smoothly and the batch is assigned without any issue.</p>\n<p>The problem exists only when creating the batch manually during the Work Order finish process.</p>\n<p>Could you please review this behavior and confirm if this is a bug or if additional configuration is required ?</p>",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/s/b4bc9f/{size}.png",
